        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173813?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Document subclassing Event as an alternative to CustomEvent</p>
<p dir="auto">Also remove "the old-fashioned way" section, as the Event constructor has been available across browsers for nearly 10 years now.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Many people don't realize that it's possible to extend the Event interface, which generally makes for a better API (removes the <code class="notranslate">.detail</code> intermediate, can possibly use <code class="notranslate">instanceof</code>). The pages that deal with "custom events" in the MDN don't mention that possibility.</p>
